WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:15.670
Unit 1 · Numbers Computers Love · done!

3
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:25.900
Unit 2 · Logic & Reasoning

4
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:31.570
Chapter 1 · True or False?

5
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:37.460
Become a logic detective!

6
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:49.240
Meet Kabir · a green TRUE card, a red FALSE card

7
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:59.950
"The sun rises in the east." → TRUE

8
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:08.240
"All birds can fly." Kabir holds up FALSE!

9
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:17.770
Why did Kabir say FALSE? Think!

10
00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:22.680
Hold that thought…

11
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:30.320
Statement = tells something you can check

12
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:39.460
TRUE = matches the facts · FALSE = doesn't

13
00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:50.910
"A cat has four legs." Check… TRUE!

14
00:01:50.910 --> 00:02:09.390
Which one can be TRUE or FALSE?

15
00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:16.830
"A week has 7 days" → a statement, TRUE

16
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:29.670
Request · Question · Shout → not statements

17
00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:44.810
No maybe! Only TRUE or FALSE

18
00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:57.520
5 + 3 = 8 → count it… TRUE

19
00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:09.630
5 + 3 = 9 → it's 8, so FALSE

20
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:21.000
"10 is odd" → 5 pairs, none left → FALSE

21
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:36.880
Quick round: true or false?

22
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:45.190
3 comes before 8 → smaller → FALSE

23
00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:55.150
A square has 4 sides → FALSE

24
00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:00.010
Cricket is played with a bat → TRUE

25
00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:12.410
Remember Kabir? Parrot, crow, sparrow… fly!

26
00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:22.240
A penguin is a bird that can't fly!

27
00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:32.050
One counter-example → "all" is FALSE

28
00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:43.900
"All" and "every" must work every time

29
00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:58.030
"All fruits are red." Which fruit breaks it?

30
00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:10.090
Banana! A yellow fruit → FALSE

31
00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:20.290
"Every number ending in 5 is odd." T or F?

32
00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:34.320
5, 15, 25 → always one left over → TRUE

33
00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:46.900
Tens pair up · the 5 leaves one alone

34
00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:55.360
Computers check TRUE or FALSE to decide

35
00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:05.880
More than 10 wins. Score 12: true or false?

36
00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:14.310
12 → TRUE, you win! 7 → FALSE, play again

37
00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:23.800
A true or false check in code = a condition

38
00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.680
Your turn: practice check

39
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:43.740
Every even number ends in 0, 2, 4, 6 or 8?

40
00:06:43.740 --> 00:07:03.170
TRUE! 14, 20, 36… no counter-example

41
00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:09.450
A statement is true or false

42
00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.800
No "maybe" in this game

43
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:16.020
One counter-example makes "all" false

44
00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:19.380
Code uses true or false to decide

45
00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:25.270
Chapter 1 done!

46
00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:32.070
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
